  - id: "#authn-cid-didkey-missing-subject"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: authn-cid-didkey-missing-subject
    label: A did:key credential without a sub claim is refused
    comment: >-
      The core authentication data model makes the sub (subject) claim REQUIRED in every
      authentication credential. The CID suite then requires sub, iss and client_id to
      share one URI, which a credential lacking one of them cannot do. Either rule refuses
      it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authentication-data-model
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693#section-2.2.2
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authn-subject-claim-uri
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authn-credential-tamper-evident-claims
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/sub-iss-client-same-uri
    steps:
      - label: the authorization server accepts did:key subjects (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${as.metadataUrl}"
          accept: application/json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /subject_identifier_types_supported
              hasValue: did:key
            - pointer: /subject_token_types_supported
              optional: true
              hasValue: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
      - label: exchange the defective credential
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${as.tokenEndpoint}"
          bodyForm:
            grant_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
            resource: "${as.realm}"
            subject_token: "${credential.didkey-missing-sub}"
            subject_token_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
        response:
          statusCode: 400
          contentType: application/json
          json:
            - pointer: /error
              equals: invalid_request

  - id: "#authn-cid-didkey-missing-issuer"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: authn-cid-didkey-missing-issuer
    label: A did:key credential without an iss claim is refused
    comment: >-
      The core authentication data model makes the iss (issuer) claim REQUIRED in every
      authentication credential. The CID suite then requires sub, iss and client_id to
      share one URI, which a credential lacking one of them cannot do. Either rule refuses
      it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
